#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/app-menu-shortcut-troubleshooting.rst:205
#: 6d3e598a5be44d48ba7467893a88d2ee
msgid "Behind the scenes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/app-menu-shortcut-troubleshooting.rst:208
#: d8b71a7f2b9243959e71bd900c249b0d
msgid ""
"``qvm-sync-appmenus`` works by invoking the *GetAppMenus* :doc:`Qubes "
"service </developer/services/qrexec>` in the target domain. This service "
"enumerates applications installed in that qube and sends formatted info back "
"to dom0 which creates ``.desktop`` files in the app qube/template directory "
"of dom0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/app-menu-shortcut-troubleshooting.rst:210
#: 9916409f7fc34487a39036b50daeef9e
msgid ""
"For Linux qubes the service script is in :file:`/etc/qubes-rpc/qubes."
"GetAppMenus``. In Windows it’s a PowerShell script located in :file:`c:"
"\\Program Files\\Invisible Things Lab\\Qubes OS Windows Tools\\qubes-rpc-"
"services\\get-appmenus.ps1` by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/app-menu-shortcut-troubleshooting.rst:212
#: b68e363c23eb460db099ad54685eaf59
msgid ""
"The list of installed applications for each app qube is stored in dom0’s :"
"file:`~/.local/share/qubes-appmenus/{<QUBE_NAME>}/apps.templates`. Each menu "
"entry is a file that follows the `.desktop file format <https://standards."
"freedesktop.org/desktop-entry-spec/desktop-entry-spec-latest.html>`__ with "
"some wildcards (``%VMNAME%``, ``%VMDIR%``). Applications selected to appear "
"in the menu are stored in :file:`~/.local/share/qubes-appmenus/{<QUBE_NAME>}/"
"apps` and in :file:`~/.local/share/applications/`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/app-menu-shortcut-troubleshooting.rst:214
